{"lines":[{"c":1,"x":0.098703609668582812,"y":0.037484954053735198,"t":"Sample Writing answers","w":0.22974924723307288,"h":0.020596548775646206},{"t":"TEST 2, WRITING TASK 1","y":0.086920669455700761,"h":0.02409270812417863,"x":0.096971429297858069,"w":0.35756718953450523,"c":1},{"h":0.020051239584093827,"w":0.69333282470703117,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 5.5 score.","c":1,"y":0.1247425211145875,"x":0.09701160455100051},{"w":0.8003252156575521,"h":0.025856531446225239,"c":1,"y":0.1517739718869392,"x":0.096921757674671011,"t":"The graph illustrats the data of different levels of annual wage of families in the united states in"},{"x":0.09683701824606876,"w":0.17519294738769531,"c":1,"y":0.17802010686611747,"t":"2007, 2011 and 2015","h":0.020252548645589896},{"w":0.82546010335286457,"c":1,"t":"As far as the number of families whose annual income was less than $25,000, it began with around","h":0.022975712476118293,"x":0.098933585856654335,"y":0.20489883009324217},{"y":0.22539781690217775,"w":0.81198211669921883,"h":0.025874494986370733,"c":1,"t":">5 million in 2007, then increased to approximately 27 million in 2011, but decreased by 2 million","x":0.098862813208461658},{"t":"4 years later. Similarly, those of families that earned $25,000 to $49,999 were about 25 million","h":0.025703306584343277,"c":1,"w":0.80027002970377603,"x":0.096962823185337471,"y":0.24599862600880229},{"w":0.81598195393880191,"t":"in 2007, after that it rose to nearly 30 million in 2011. Finally it decreased to around 27 million in","h":0.02829532445034133,"y":0.26600276812164603,"c":1,"x":0.096843879115702317},{"h":0.017441859497830947,"c":1,"w":0.048543688456217454,"x":0.097087379242765059,"t":"2015.","y":0.29505813980050322},{"x":0.098963562218744791,"y":0.32119047320240091,"c":1,"t":"By contrast, the groups of families which have high income, including $75,000 to $99.999 and","w":0.77879140218098952,"h":0.023128640243197607},{"y":0.34208957014098729,"x":0.098874643109171198,"w":0.64879089355468744,"t":"$100,000 or more, experienced a drop in 2011, but their data went up in 2015.","h":0.02365852902611465,"c":1},{"t":"Interesting things could be seen in the group of middle income, the data remain the same in 2007,","c":1,"w":0.8293172200520833,"x":0.096974407099742921,"y":0.37114033909821931,"h":0.024800925091419623},{"y":0.39671222193377953,"h":0.017622067698065846,"c":1,"x":0.099006201731271323,"w":0.12237594604492187,"t":"2011 and 2015."},{"h":0.014641744548286595,"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:","x":0.10097087899841715,"y":0.43457943919243402,"w":0.31067960103352865,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.46801273518494035,"t":"This response does present most of the data within the bar chart and the key","x":0.14551159051893686,"w":0.72450754801432282,"h":0.021487132039768264},{"t":"teatures required.","y":0.48928278457571051,"h":0.01934590503062783,"c":1,"x":0.14344628215670188,"w":0.17322766621907551},{"c":1,"y":0.52596636155898202,"h":0.018382818750874663,"t":"To improve the response, an overview of the information should be included,","x":0.14751193711138549,"w":0.71854746500651046},{"x":0.14368931874643504,"y":0.54505813961828864,"h":0.016001050123173099,"c":1,"w":0.74951456705729158,"t":"for example: Across the 8 years, households with incomes below $50,000 rose,"},{"x":0.14362991927010096,"w":0.75159128824869792,"c":1,"t":"then fell back slightly, households with incomes of over $75,000 fell slightly then","h":0.01993258823858246,"y":0.56206685669860401},{"c":1,"x":0.14364368033306818,"t":"increased and those with the mid-level incomes remained the same.","y":0.58189755353957873,"w":0.64474838256835942,"h":0.017240843371810199},{"w":0.72249689737955725,"c":1,"h":0.020574304693584566,"x":0.14749360346297824,"y":0.61831005043872056,"t":"The information is arranged coherently, starting with the details for the lower-"},{"h":0.022029824420299104,"y":0.6363530154799546,"w":0.78853663126627593,"c":1,"t":"income households, then the higher, then the mid-section. There are some effective","x":0.14361559038961758},{"y":0.65697674406719386,"c":1,"w":0.49320388793945302,"h":0.017478084861303755,"x":0.14757281334326464,"t":"cohesive devices [As far as | Similarly | By contrast]."},{"x":0.14742938832488392,"c":1,"t":"The vocabulary is suitable for the task, but there is an error [>5 million \/ 25 million]","y":0.69063882883178385,"w":0.77311650594075521,"h":0.022534760804933884},{"y":0.71366279058238768,"x":0.14757282087937759,"t":"which is not helpful when reporting the details.","w":0.43883494059244788,"h":0.017489857539952358,"c":1},{"y":0.74849500679860836,"c":1,"w":0.71857955932617179,"t":"There is a mix of simple and complex structures, with sentences that contain","h":0.020163177775445407,"x":0.14751255027875573},{"c":1,"h":0.02143214573369967,"w":0.7866535949707032,"t":"multiple clauses. There are some examples of missing capitalisation [united states \/","x":0.14940149595857161,"y":0.76593557303241688},{"t":"United States] with some errors [remain \/ remained].","c":1,"x":0.14942978860438472,"w":0.49335220336914065,"h":0.018547400952870996,"y":0.7872300705568076},{"y":0.82322257241343355,"c":1,"w":0.74578699747721366,"x":0.14751500965831033,"h":0.020564236744913367,"t":"To improve the response, it is important to re-read to check for small errors with"},{"t":"vocabulary and to include an overview or summary of the salient information.","h":0.023499664116499952,"c":1,"y":0.8391406964778142,"w":0.72647232055664057,"x":0.14740545893840837},{"h":0.01308139551465759,"t":"130","c":1,"x":0.10291262197199061,"y":0.95639534871582432,"w":0.036893202463785801}],"w":2400,"h":3209}